  "summary": "A rotor assembly is the complete rotating part of a machine — here a multistage pump rotor: shaft, impellers, interstage sleeves, balance drum, thrust collar, locknuts and coupling hub. Each part is fitted in sequence with controlled fits, keys and stack-up; the assembled rotor is then dynamically balanced in two planes before it goes into the casing.",
